        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "08a6ad7d-e66e-50d9-a900-c28ae716a527",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leon Uris\n- Products: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, Exodus, Trinity, The Haj\n- Places: Berlin, Germany, East Berlin, East Germany\n- Events: World War II, Berlin Airlift\n- Topics: historical fiction\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Marcus Uris was born on August 3, 1924, and became an American author known for historical fiction.\n- Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\n- Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin vividly describes the Berlin Airlift and interactions among people from the five nations involved, including the three major Western Allies and the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Exodus in 1958.\n- Leon Uris published the bestselling book Trinity in 1976.\n- Leon Uris published The Haj in 1984.\n- The Haj is a novel about a Palestinian Arab family caught up in the region's historic events of the 1920s through the 1950s, as witnessed by Ishmael, the youngest son.\n- Leon Marcus Uris died on June 21, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
